        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be fixed on latest `main`.\r\n\r\nThe issue was not in scrolling per se, but the fact that its drawing was (somehow) blocked by cursor animation. I noticed it because disabling cursor animation made things work. \"Works on first scroll\" was also an indicator of this as cursor animation is not done on first move.\r\n\r\nThis problem in this issue manifested itself because cursor animation was done *on every line between start and end positions*. As each step was about 0.00096 milliseconds on 260000 line jump and [timers not working on sub-millisecond delay](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ad46fda7862153107124f95d4ea0e510eafc1dd8/doc/mini-animate.txt#L504-L509) there were a lot of steps (about 1040) which were done \"immediately\". As each step is \"delete extmark and add extmark\", this somehow resulted into blocking the scroll redraw.\r\n\r\nThe solution here is to limit the number of steps in cursor animation. This is technically breaking, but nothing serious should be visible on user side (hopefully).",
